India holds the 9th position among nations most severely impacted by climate-related catastrophes over the past three decades, as highlighted by the newest Climate Risk Index (CRI) report published by Germanwatch, an NGO headquartered in Bonn. The report, developed through an analysis of current and past climate data, was unveiled on the second day of the ongoing COP30 climate conference.

