The downpours resulted from two tropical storms converging near the western coast, succeeding a wet season that left rivers swollen and terrain precarious. "Nothing remains. It obliterated homes, destroyed the bridge, and demolished everything. The sole structures still intact were the church and the warehouse where we had taken shelter," said Stephanie Ramírez, a 21-year-old helicopter rescuee.

