As one inhaled sharply, worried that the events of 2013 were unfolding once more, memories of that time, when the state was expected to learn and transform, flooded the mind. In June of that year, torrential rains unleashed devastating flash floods from Kedarnath to Rishikesh, causing thousands of villages to endure hardship and resulting in over 5,000 individuals reported missing. The harrowing visuals reveal how a cloudburst in a mountainous area can unleash devastation, gathering overwhelming force as it races through valleys and steep inclines, rendering control utterly impossible.

