The Indian Meteorological Department (IMD) has indicated that light rain will continue throughout the coming week, with no forecast for heavy, widespread rainfall in the short term. Director Mrutyunjay Mohapatra highlighted the potential emergence of a new low-pressure system in the Bay of Bengal, which may develop wind gusts, although a cyclone is improbable at this time.

